    "scope": "Current Connect public native SDK library unit methods plus compilation of all server test consumers after RTP-only API removal. Root release profile, isolated fixtures/state. No actual Connect native/browser clock interoperability, live AV or operating qualification from compilation or unit methods."
  },
  "behavior": [
    "Public CanonicalClient send_native_media_datagram/receive_native_media_datagram accept bounded RTP or clock-only SR/SDES and preserve original wire bytes. The former RTP-only names are removed; every SDK/server fixture caller is migrated without compatibility aliases. Public canonical wire helper reexports avoid direct upstream IO in examples.",
    "The audio-only private PCMU reader checks the exact owned handle, consumes clock metadata separately and returns only160-byte PT0frames. One original absolute deadline survives continuous metadata; timeout/cancellation does not close the signed physical peer. It does not implement native AV presentation.",
    "Two actual local TLS QUIC methods use controlled post-auth clients and signed control replies, current private-audio handle fixtures and fully joined owned endpoints. Clock metadata precedes actual PCM; foreign-handle metadata refuses while the peer remains open. At least three clock-only datagrams are emitted before an80msread; continuing reports cannot extend that original deadline past the external300msguard. These are client-boundary tests, not service enrollment/authentication/current engine admission or full runtime profiles.",
    "The browser/native functional actor now declares the clock profile, emits common-CNAME/NTP audio/video reports only after successful actual RTP submissions and counts real RTP payload packets/octets. Both tracks sample the same monotonic epoch; reports have no idle timer. Received current-binding reports are bounded and kept separate from decoded media/readiness. Runtime073 now passes three of four short native methods; captured EdDSA fails original subscription before media ingress. See browser-client-native-clock-runtime.json. It remains preencoded/offline-decoded, not live native encoding/playout."
  ],
